  "texts": [
    {
      "id": "uece-2022-1-f2-english-t1",
      "label": "Texto 1",
      "title": "T E X T",
      "lines": [
        {
          "number": null,
          "text": "Children set for more climate disasters than"
        },
        {
          "number": null,
          "text": "their grandparents, research shows"
        },
        {
          "number": 1,
          "text": "People born today will suffer many"
        },
        {
          "number": 2,
          "text": "times more extreme heatwaves and"
        },
        {
          "number": 3,
          "text": "other climate disasters over their"
        },
        {
          "number": 4,
          "text": "lifetimes than their grandparents,"
        },
        {
          "number": 5,
          "text": "research has shown. The study is the"
        },
        {
          "number": 6,
          "text": "first to assess the contrasting"
        },
        {
          "number": 7,
          "text": "experience of climate extremes by"
        },
        {
          "number": 8,
          "text": "different age groups and starkly"
        },
        {
          "number": 9,
          "text": "highlights the intergenerational"
        },
        {
          "number": 10,
          "text": "injustice posed by the climate crisis."
        },
        {
          "number": 11,
          "text": "The analysis showed that a child"
        },
        {
          "number": 12,
          "text": "born in 2020 will endure an average of"
        },
        {
          "number": 13,
          "text": "30 extreme heatwaves in their lifetime,"
        },
        {
          "number": 14,
          "text": "even if countries fulfil their current"
        },
        {
          "number": 15,
          "text": "pledges to cut future carbon emissions."
        },
        {
          "number": 16,
          "text": "That is seven times more heatwaves"
        },
        {
          "number": 17,
          "text": "than someone born in 1960. Today’s"
        },
        {
          "number": 18,
          "text": "babies will also grow up to experience"
        },
        {
          "number": 19,
          "text": "twice as many droughts and wildfires"
        },
        {
          "number": 20,
          "text": "and three times more river floods and"
        },
        {
          "number": 21,
          "text": "crop failures than someone who is 60"
        },
        {
          "number": 22,
          "text": "years old today."
        },
        {
          "number": 23,
          "text": "However, rapidly cutting global"
        },
        {
          "number": 24,
          "text": "emissions to keep global heating to"
        },
        {
          "number": 25,
          "text": "1.5C would almost halve the heatwaves"
        },
        {
          "number": 26,
          "text": "today’s children will experience, while"
        },
        {
          "number": 27,
          "text": "keeping under 2C would reduce the"
        },
        {
          "number": 28,
          "text": "number by a quarter."
        },
        {
          "number": 29,
          "text": "A vital task of the UN’s Cop26"
        },
        {
          "number": 30,
          "text": "climate summit in Glasgow in November"
        },
        {
          "number": 31,
          "text": "is to deliver pledges of bigger emissions"
        },
        {
          "number": 32,
          "text": "cuts from the most polluting countries"
        },
        {
          "number": 33,
          "text": "and climate justice will be an important"
        },
        {
          "number": 34,
          "text": "element of the negotiations. Developing"
        },
        {
          "number": 35,
          "text": "countries, and the youth strike"
        },
        {
          "number": 36,
          "text": "protesters who have taken to the"
        },
        {
          "number": 37,
          "text": "streets around the world, point out that"
        },
        {
          "number": 38,
          "text": "those who did least to cause the climate"
        },
        {
          "number": 39,
          "text": "crisis are suffering the most."
        },
        {
          "number": 40,
          "text": "“Our results highlight a severe"
        },
        {
          "number": 41,
          "text": "threat to the safety of young"
        },
        {
          "number": 42,
          "text": "generations and call for drastic emission"
        },
        {
          "number": 43,
          "text": "reductions to safeguard their future,”"
        },
        {
          "number": 44,
          "text": "said Prof Wim Thiery, at Vrije"
        },
        {
          "number": null,
          "text": "7"
        },
        {
          "number": 45,
          "text": "Universiteit Brussel in Belgium and who"
        },
        {
          "number": 46,
          "text": "led the research. He said people under"
        },
        {
          "number": 47,
          "text": "40 today were set to live"
        },
        {
          "number": 48,
          "text": "“unprecedented” lives, ie suffering"
        },
        {
          "number": 49,
          "text": "heatwaves, droughts, floods and crop"
        },
        {
          "number": 50,
          "text": "failures that would have been virtually"
        },
        {
          "number": 51,
          "text": "impossible – 0.01% chance – without"
        },
        {
          "number": 52,
          "text": "global heating."
        },
        {
          "number": 53,
          "text": "Dr Katja Frieler, at the Potsdam"
        },
        {
          "number": 54,
          "text": "Institute for Climate Impact Research in"
        },
        {
          "number": 55,
          "text": "Germany and part of the study team,"
        },
        {
          "number": 56,
          "text": "said: “The good news is we can take"
        },
        {
          "number": 57,
          "text": "much of the climate burden from our"
        },
        {
          "number": 58,
          "text": "children’s shoulders if we limit warming"
        },
        {
          "number": 59,
          "text": "to 1.5C by phasing out fossil fuel use."
        },
        {
          "number": 60,
          "text": "This is a huge opportunity.”"
        },
        {
          "number": 61,
          "text": "Leo Hickman, editor of Carbon"
        },
        {
          "number": 62,
          "text": "Brief, said: “These new findings"
        },
        {
          "number": 63,
          "text": "reinforce our 2019 analysis which"
        },
        {
          "number": 64,
          "text": "showed that today’s children will need"
        },
        {
          "number": 65,
          "text": "to emit eight times less CO2 over the"
        },
        {
          "number": 66,
          "text": "course of their lifetime than their"
        },
        {
          "number": 67,
          "text": "grandparents, if global warming is to be"
        },
        {
          "number": 68,
          "text": "kept below 1.5C. Climate change is"
        },
        {
          "number": 69,
          "text": "already exacerbating many injustices,"
        },
        {
          "number": 70,
          "text": "but the intergenerational injustice of"
        },
        {
          "number": 71,
          "text": "climate change is particularly stark.”"
        },
        {
          "number": 72,
          "text": "The research, published in the"
        },
        {
          "number": 73,
          "text": "journal Science, combined extreme"
        },
        {
          "number": 74,
          "text": "event projections from sophisticated"
        },
        {
          "number": 75,
          "text": "computer climate models, detailed"
        },
        {
          "number": 76,
          "text": "population and life expectancy data,"
        },
        {
          "number": 77,
          "text": "and global temperature trajectories"
        },
        {
          "number": 78,
          "text": "from the Intergovernmental Panel on"
        },
        {
          "number": 79,
          "text": "Climate Change."
        },
        {
          "number": 80,
          "text": "The scientists said the increases"
        },
        {
          "number": 81,
          "text": "in climate impacts calculated for today’s"
        },
        {
          "number": 82,
          "text": "young people were likely to be"
        },
        {
          "number": 83,
          "text": "underestimates, as multiple extremes"
        },
        {
          "number": 84,
          "text": "within a year had to be grouped"
        },
        {
          "number": 85,
          "text": "together and the greater intensity of"
        },
        {
          "number": 86,
          "text": "events was not accounted for."
        },
        {
          "number": 87,
          "text": "There was significant regional"
        },
        {
          "number": 88,
          "text": "variation in the results. For example,"
        },
        {
          "number": 89,
          "text": "the 53 million children born in Europe"
        },
        {
          "number": 90,
          "text": "and central Asia between 2016 and"
        },
        {
          "number": 91,
          "text": "2020 will experience about four times"
        },
        {
          "number": 92,
          "text": "more extreme events in their lifetimes"
        },
        {
          "number": 93,
          "text": "under current emissions pledges, but"
        },
        {
          "number": 94,
          "text": "the 172 million children of the same age"
        },
        {
          "number": 95,
          "text": "in sub-Saharan Africa face 5.7 times"
        },
        {
          "number": 96,
          "text": "more extreme events."
        },
        {
          "number": 97,
          "text": "“This highlights a disproportionate"
        },
        {
          "number": 98,
          "text": "climate change burden for young"
        },
        {
          "number": 99,
          "text": "generations in the global south,” the"
        },
        {
          "number": 100,
          "text": "researchers said."
        },
        {
          "number": 101,
          "text": "Dohyeon Kim, an activist from"
        },
        {
          "number": 102,
          "text": "South Korea who took part in the global"
        },
        {
          "number": 103,
          "text": "climate strike on Friday, said:"
        },
        {
          "number": 104,
          "text": "“Countries of the global north need to"
        },
        {
          "number": 105,
          "text": "push governments to put justice and"
        },
        {
          "number": 106,
          "text": "equity at the heart of climate action,"
        },
        {
          "number": 107,
          "text": "both in terms of climate [aid] and"
        },
        {
          "number": 108,
          "text": "setting more ambitious pledges that"
        },
        {
          "number": 109,
          "text": "take into consideration historical"
        },
        {
          "number": 110,
          "text": "responsibilities.”"
        },
        {
          "number": 111,
          "text": "The analysis found that only those"
        },
        {
          "number": 112,
          "text": "aged under 40 years today will live to"
        },
        {
          "number": 113,
          "text": "see the consequences of the choices"
        },
        {
          "number": 114,
          "text": "made on emissions cuts. Those who are"
        },
        {
          "number": 115,
          "text": "older will have died before the impacts"
        },
        {
          "number": 116,
          "text": "of those choices become apparent in the"
        },
        {
          "number": 117,
          "text": "world."
        },
        {
          "number": null,
          "text": "https://www.theguardian.com/environment/"
